id: jacket
name: Jacket
kind: crafting
categories: standard-clothing
slots: 1
# "This piece of Apparel can be worn over Armor" - the one exception to Armor's "you cannot
# equip any piece of Apparel while wearing Armor". Read by the Layers.
wornOverArmor: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Soak Value 1(bT) higher, and it can go on over Armor.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: one line to an effect, each opening with
# its tag as the rulebook writes one - [Passive], [Automatic, 1/Encounter].
summary: >
  [Passive]: Soak Value 1(bT) higher.

  [Passive]: Can be worn over Armor.
text: >
  Jacket: A piece of clothing designed to protect another piece of clothing underneath.
  –Apparel Category: Standard Clothing
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: Increase your Soak Value by 1(bT). This piece of Apparel can be worn over Armor.

---

# The Soak Value is the wearer's, while worn. Going on over Armor is the Layers' to allow: they
# come with the rest of the Apparel rules, and read `wornOverArmor`.
[passive]
soakValue += 1(bT);
